From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] faudio: An effect's reference count changes atomically.

FAPOBase_AddRef and FAPOBase_Release changed m_lReferenceCount with plain += and -=, and Release read it back
afterwards. Every effect Wine builds on FAPOBase (reverb, volume meter, the XAPOFX effects) shares that count between
the game's references and those its voices hold, so a game that attaches one effect to voices it creates and destroys
on more than one thread loses updates between them: the count reaches zero while a voice still holds the effect and
the mixer reads freed memory (XAPOFXParams_GetParameters, from a voice's GetEffectParameters). The count now changes
atomically, as XAPOBase's does with InterlockedIncrement on Windows, and Release returns the value it computed.

The problem was found by reading bornaradusin/PC5 (LGPL-2.1-or-later; patch 0002 of its patches/prospero-win); this
change is written independently here (NOTICE.md, "PC5").
---
 libs/faudio/src/FAPOBase.c | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/faudio/src/FAPOBase.c b/libs/faudio/src/FAPOBase.c
index 27a98e1..c3c8353 100644
--- a/libs/faudio/src/FAPOBase.c
+++ b/libs/faudio/src/FAPOBase.c
@@ -104,21 +104,21 @@ void CreateFAPOBaseWithCustomAllocatorEXT(
 	fapo->m_lReferenceCount = 1;
 }
 
+/* The count changes atomically, as XAPOBase's does with InterlockedIncrement. A game attaches one effect to voices it
+ * creates and destroys on several threads; an update lost between them frees the effect while a voice still holds it. */
 int32_t FAPOBase_AddRef(FAPOBase *fapo)
 {
-	fapo->m_lReferenceCount += 1;
-	return fapo->m_lReferenceCount;
+	return __atomic_add_fetch(&fapo->m_lReferenceCount, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
 }
 
 int32_t FAPOBase_Release(FAPOBase *fapo)
 {
-	fapo->m_lReferenceCount -= 1;
-	if (fapo->m_lReferenceCount == 0)
+	int32_t count = __atomic_sub_fetch(&fapo->m_lReferenceCount, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+	if (count == 0)
 	{
 		fapo->Destructor(fapo);
-		return 0;
 	}
-	return fapo->m_lReferenceCount;
+	return count;
 }
 
 uint32_t FAPOBase_GetRegistrationProperties(
